                "fields"
              ],
              "type": "object"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "Record"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "A declaration-bound membership semi-join as a composable boolean\nexpression kind — the form the `eventMembers.memberOf(...)` /\n`hasRole(...)` rule helpers and the `ctx.permissions.<decl>.requireRole`\ntwin lower to (LLP 0053 §Agent-auth item 1 admits it as a new\ndeclarative IR expression kind).\n\nIt is **authoritative-only**: unlike every other variant it cannot be\nanswered by the pure `ValueExpr` evaluator, because deciding it requires\na non-recursive storage semi-join over the membership table (bypassing\nthat table's row-visibility rules). The pure evaluator therefore refuses\nit (`SNAPBACK_VALUE_EXPR_AUTHORITATIVE_ONLY`), the query path answers it\nthrough `QueryPlan::membership_filters` / the `ctx.permissions` read, and\nthe derived optimistic overlay refuses rather than mirrors it — so a\nrole check is server-decided, never optimistically forged client-side.\n\n@ref LLP 0056#rule-helpers — the declaration-bound membership predicate.",
          "properties": {
            "MembershipExists": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/MembershipPredicate"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "MembershipExists"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        }
      ]
